    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d297-a1">

                <pb facs="0591" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg495"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to General Schenck.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1874-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2,
                        1874</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your letter of the 7th of
                    June last, respecting the establishment by your Government of stations in New
                    Zealand for the observation of the transit of Venus, I have the honor to
                    transmit to you herewith, for your information, copy of a letter and of its
                    inclosures which I have received from the secretary of state for the colonies on
                    this subject.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
